# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Claude Code
# Agent worktrees are full checkouts, each with its own node_modules — a stray
# `git add -A` while one exists would try to commit ~700MB. Personal settings
# are per-machine. Everything else under .claude/ (settings.json, agents/,
# skills/, commands/) is shared project config and stays committable, which
# matters here: this repo is teaching material, and how the agents are set up
# is part of what's being taught.
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json

# Superpowers brainstorm scratch
# Each session spins up a local server and drops its pid, port, log and
# instance id under state/. Pure runtime, and it turns up as a dozen untracked
# files in the IDE. Generated pages under content/ are deliberately NOT ignored
# — those are output, and worth keeping or binning on purpose rather than by
# default.
.superpowers/**/state/
.superpowers/**/.last-*

# Planning docs — kept local
# CONTENT.md carries seat counts, the student allocation and cross-promotion
# plans that are the organiser's to announce, not this repo's to publish.
# COPY.md is the working copy deck. Both stay on disk; neither is tracked.
CONTENT.md
COPY.md
